    <span class="section-label">Comparing your options</span>
    <h1>AI website builders vs. <em>a custom-coded site built to bring in calls</em></h1>
    <p>Wix AI, Squarespace AI, Hostinger AI, Durable, GoDaddy AIO, and many others promise a business website in 30 seconds, and they can give you a free draft that fast. This page compares whether that draft puts paying customers on your calendar or only looks as if it could.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container prose" style="max-width:980px">

    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Where an AI builder is the right call</h2>
    <p>An AI builder is useful as a one-day research step while you work out what you want. You can generate a free draft and see whether its rough shape matches your idea. If a blank page has you stuck, an AI starter can get you moving. A draft, though, isn't yet a site that brings in customers.</p>

    <h2>Where AI builders cost you leads</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Generic copy.</strong> AI builders learn from existing template content, so your About page sounds like every other plumber's. Generic copy ranks worse on Google over time, and Google's helpful-content updates target it directly.</li>
      <li><strong>The platform's speed.</strong> Wix AI sites get Wix speed (50&ndash;70 on Google's speed test for phones), and Squarespace AI sites get Squarespace speed (60&ndash;75). The AI changes how the template is filled in, not how fast it loads.</li>
      <li><strong>Shallow local search.</strong> AI-written business details for Google (schema) are often wrong, and contact details often come from outdated public data. AI-made city pages are the copy-and-paste kind (doorway pages) that Google increasingly penalizes.</li>
      <li><strong>Generic forms.</strong> Every AI build gets the same name, email, and message form. It doesn't ask about the trade, flag urgent jobs, or fit how you dispatch work.</li>
      <li><strong>A template underneath.</strong> Most AI builders take your trade, name, and location, then fill a template with generated copy and sometimes stock-style photos. It's the same template engine they had two years ago with a chatbot on top, so the hosting, speed, and ranking are unchanged.</li>
    </ul>

