    <h2>What one extra call a week is worth</h2>
    <p>An AI site looks done, with headings, photos, and a contact form in place. Looking done isn't the same as ranking, loading fast on a phone, or turning visitors into calls. The gap is easy to miss, because the site looks fine in the editor.</p>
    <p>In a worked example for a typical local business, a $500 average job and one extra call a week come to $26,000 a year in potential work. At $5,000 a job, it's 10 times that. "Good enough" can't rank first in your area's map results or win the click against a sharper competitor. The leads it never brings in never show up on a bill.</p>

